ctory _x_ ˆ0: _T_ is contained within _X_<sup>~~ˆ~~</sup> 0: _T_ . \n\n**Theorem 1 (CKRS Coverage Guarantee)** _Let X_<sup>~~ˆ~~</sup> 0: _T be the KRS defined in_ (7) _and let_ ¯ _et_ = [¯ _et,_ 1 _, . . . ,_ ¯ _et,n_ ]<sup>_⊤_</sup> _∈_ R<sup>_n_</sup> _. Define the conformalized Koopman reachable set (CKRS) as_ \n\n\n\n_where_ diag(¯ _et_ ) _∈_ R<sup>_n×n_</sup> _is a diagonal matrix with e_ ¯ _t on its diagonal. Then, for a new reference trajectory x_<sup>_ref_</sup> 0: _T_<sup>_,_(0)</sup> _drawn from the same distribution, the CKRS contains true closed-loop system trajectory generated by_ (1b) _with probability at least_ 1 _− δ:_ \n\n\n\n**Proof** The proof combines a deterministic containment guarantee with a probabilistic coverage guarantee. \n\n15 \n\n"
